From: SiliconLoop closed-loop development
Subject: [PATCH 0019] ai-agent: print the recover_task verdict into the serial log

Incremental on 0017 (tool_recover.c is new there). The serial log records
tool results as byte counts only ("Tool recover_task result: 101 bytes"),
so recovery rounds left no verdict evidence on the wire - the only sinks
were the LLM conversation and actions.log on tmpfs, both unreachable
after the round. The verdict is a designed public one-liner (<=256 B):
log it in full via syslog.

Verified 2026-11-04: B rounds now carry "[recover] verdict {...}"
lines that scenario.py counts (see docs/evidence/2026-11-04/).
--- a/src/tools/tool_recover.c
+++ b/src/tools/tool_recover.c
@@ -280,9 +280,24 @@
 
 /* ── tool entry ─────────────────────────────────────────────────── */
 
+static int tool_recover_execute_inner(const char *input_json, char *output,
+    size_t output_size);
+
 int tool_recover_execute(const char *input_json, char *output,
     size_t output_size)
 {
+    /* SiliconLoop: the serial log records tool results as byte counts
+     * only, but this verdict is the acceptance evidence for recovery
+     * rounds and is a designed public one-liner (<=256 B). Print it in
+     * full so every round's serial log carries it. */
+    int rc = tool_recover_execute_inner(input_json, output, output_size);
+    syslog(LOG_INFO, "[%s] verdict %s\n", TAG, output);
+    return rc;
+}
+
